1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,760
text: #01 WHEN I RETURNED HOME, 
I'D BECOME A HERO

2
00:00:06,230 --> 00:00:07,510
Goran: Did we do it?

3
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:10,380
Eric: Looks like the demons have retreated.

4
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:12,760
Goran: We didn't finish off the Demon King, 

5
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:15,750
text: GORAN, THE WARRIOR

6
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:15,750
Goran: but we messed him up good.

7
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:20,400
text: ERIC, THE HERO

8
00:00:16,149 --> 00:00:17,340
Eric: Yeah.

9
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:20,390
Eric: I doubt he'll try anything 
else for a while.

10
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:22,980
Luck: If I could convert this into mana...

11
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:25,220
Eric: I guess all three of us 
will make it home.

12
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:26,400
Goran: Guess so.

13
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:30,760
Luck: Or maybe that won't work unless 
the rest of him dies too?

14
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:31,650
Eric: Luck?

15
00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:36,280
Luck: Maybe if I amplify the 
scant remnants... Or not?

16
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,520
Eric: Some things never change.

17
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:42,780
Goran: We drove off the Demon King, 
and you're still fixated on that arm?

18
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:43,690
Luck: Huh?

19
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:47,660
Luck: Sorry, wasn't listening. 
You say something?

20
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:51,020
Goran: This sort of thing's why you 
can never get a girlfriend.

21
00:00:52,490 --> 00:00:57,580
Goran: Well, it's time we said goodbye 
to this gloomy dimensional rift.

22
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,900
Goran: That was one long battle.

23
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:04,319
Eric: It took even longer than I expected.

24
00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:07,890
Eric: Too bad I had to miss out 
on the birth of my child.

25
00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:11,980
Goran: And I won't be surprised if my daughter's 
forgotten what I look like.

26
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:15,370
Luck: The worries never end 
when you have a family.

27
00:01:15,370 --> 00:01:16,870
Luck: I'll just stay single.

28
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:22,250
Goran: Nah, Luck. Having a family 
waiting for you is a wonderful thing.

29
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:27,200
Eric: That's right. Goran and I managed to keep 
fighting because we have that support.

30
00:01:28,110 --> 00:01:31,080
Eric: You better hurry up and 
make a family of your own.

31
00:01:39,590 --> 00:01:41,480
Goran: Man, you gotta be joking.

32
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,850
Eric: There are still that many demons?

33
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:54,180
Goran: Oh well. Time to go on a rampage.

34
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:59,120
Eric: Looks like I'll have to wait a 
little longer to meet my kid.

35
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,280
Luck: We're already totally battle weary.

36
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:04,740
Luck: We'll never survive a head-on fight.

37
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:06,700
Luck: And so...

38
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:10,000
Luck: Eric, Goran.

39
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:14,880
Luck: Leave this to me, and get out of here!

40
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:24,300
Goran: What're you saying, Luck?!

41
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:26,880
Eric: You want us to leave you here, 
and run for it?!

42
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,380
Luck: The Demon King hasn't been defeated yet.

43
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:31,900
Luck: Once he rises again, we're going 
to need the hero's strength!

44
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:35,270
Goran: Then that doesn't concern me, 
the warrior. I'll fight too!

45
00:02:35,620 --> 00:02:37,520
Luck: Don't you have a family to go see?

46
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,770
Eric: Luck! Stop showing off!

47
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:42,530
Eric: Earth magic?

48
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:43,400
Goran: Luck!

49
00:02:44,010 --> 00:02:46,910
Goran: Damn! He cast a barrier spell on it!

50
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:50,480
Goran: Quick screwing around, Luck! 
Cancel this spell!

51
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,670
Eric: We can't leave you here alone!

52
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:56,290
Luck: You said your families are what's 
supported you in battle.

53
00:02:56,730 --> 00:03:00,180
Luck: To me, you guys are like family.

54
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,480
Eric: Luck...

55
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:03,170
Luck: I'll catch up soon enough.

56
00:03:03,170 --> 00:03:06,930
Luck: You guys know how stubborn I can be.

57
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:12,880
Luck: Having you nearby will be too distracting
to fight all those demon enemies.

58
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:14,180
Luck: Please...

59
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:17,700
Luck: Go!

60
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:19,130
Eric: Luck!

61
00:03:19,130 --> 00:03:22,540
Goran: Don't die on us!

62
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:32,580
Luck: Now come and get me, demons!

63
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:36,960
Luck: Don't think it'll be easy to get past me!

64
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:39,750
Luck: Let's do this!

65
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:47,470
Luck: The demons just won't stop coming.

66
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:52,250
Luck: I guess... this is my... limit.

67
00:03:53,490 --> 00:03:57,160
Luck: That's when I suddenly 
reached a turning point.

68
00:03:57,480 --> 00:04:00,480
text: DEMON GENERAL

69
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:04,240
Luck: M-My energy...

70
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:08,050
Luck: My life force is... being absorbed?

71
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:09,750
Luck: It must be Drain Touch!

72
00:04:13,490 --> 00:04:16,230
Luck: There went most of my mana, too.

73
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:27,640
Luck: Right back at you!

74
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:30,130
Luck: Drain Touch!

75
00:04:44,410 --> 00:04:48,400
Luck: My Learning skill allows me to pick up
 any spell that's used against me.

76
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:52,170
Luck: This'll let me recover and 
replenish at the same time.

77
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:01,160
Luck: Bring it on!

78
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:03,760
Luck: I feel like now, I could fight for years!

79
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,930
Luck: How many weeks...

80
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:11,890
Luck: No, how many months have I been fighting?

81
00:05:11,890 --> 00:05:13,770
Luck: I've lost track of time.

82
00:05:14,410 --> 00:05:18,820
Luck: Whenever I got sleepy, 
I'd self-cast a spell called Marionette.

83
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:23,520
Luck: By using that, my body would 
keep fighting on while I slept.

84
00:05:24,650 --> 00:05:28,180
Luck: I barely even felt like 
I was human anymore.

85
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:41,690
Luck: Did I... kill them... all?

86
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:00,690
Luck: Recovered already, have you?

87
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:05,340
Luck: That was quick, 

88
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,760
Luck: Demon King!

89
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:14,480
Luck: I thought it'd take you a decade. 
Or at least several years.

90
00:06:16,370 --> 00:06:20,450
Luck: I'll start by fighting in close, 
and keep him from using his fiery magic!

91
00:06:24,870 --> 00:06:26,580
Luck: Drain Touch!

92
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:37,060
Luck: This wound's more serious than I thought!

93
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:38,880
Luck: I'm in trouble if I don't recover soon!

94
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:49,280
Luck: I'd expect nothing less of 
the Demon King's Hexblade.

95
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:53,480
Luck: Who needs a sword?! I'm a sorcerer!

96
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,740
Luck: Imprisoning Hellfire!

97
00:06:58,620 --> 00:07:00,080
Luck: Imprisoning Hellfire!

98
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:02,350
Luck: Drain Touch!

99
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:07,910
Luck: I knew it.

100
00:07:07,910 --> 00:07:12,010
Luck: You're too busy defending 
against Imprisoning Hellfire

101
00:07:12,010 --> 00:07:14,640
Luck: to do anything about Drain Touch!

102
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:16,590
Luck: Time to choose!

103
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:19,160
Luck: Will Imprisoning Hellfire 
burn you to a crisp, 

104
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:21,650
Luck: or will you lose all your life force?!

105
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:45,400
Luck: Did... I do it?

106
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:56,230
Luck: Oh, yeah!

107
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:07,500
Luck: Now then, where am I?

108
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:10,980
Luck: Well, following that road 
will take me somewhere.

109
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:16,790
Luck: Great. I'm broke, and my 
adventurer card burned up.

110
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:28,870
Luck: This is the royal capital... isn't it?

111
00:08:34,090 --> 00:08:36,380
guard 1: H-Hey, stop right there!

112
00:08:37,299 --> 00:08:38,559
Luck: What's the matter?

113
00:08:42,299 --> 00:08:43,970
Luck: They even gave me clothes.

114
00:08:43,970 --> 00:08:46,390
Luck: Talk about nice guys.

115
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:50,730
Luck: Well, I'll start by dropping 
by Goran's place.

116
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:53,760
Luck: I-It's huge!

117
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,500
Butler: May I help you?

118
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:57,780
Luck: Um...

119
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:00,670
Luck: I'd like to see Goran.

120
00:09:00,670 --> 00:09:01,920
Butler: Do you have an appointment?

121
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:03,780
Luck: No, I'm afraid I don't.

122
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:07,540
Butler: I cannot allow you in, if you lack one.

123
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:10,170
Luck: If you tell him Luck is here, 
he'll understand.

124
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:13,330
Butler: We get your kind here quite often.

125
00:09:13,330 --> 00:09:14,840
Luck: I'm telling the truth!

126
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:16,180
Butler: Please take your leave.

127
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:19,030
Luck: Phooey.

128
00:09:20,030 --> 00:09:21,660
Luck: Whatever.

129
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:26,000
Luck: Next, I'll go to the guild, 
and get my adventurer card reissued.

130
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:32,610
Luck: That stone statue didn't 
used to be there.

131
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:36,070
Luck: He's a sorcerer, huh?

132
00:09:36,450 --> 00:09:38,920
Luck: And a handsome one, at that.

133
00:09:40,030 --> 00:09:41,150
Luck: Excuse me.

134
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:41,980
passerby 1: Huh?

135
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:44,160
Luck: Who is this a statue of?

136
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:46,980
passerby 1: What?! You don't know?!

137
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:48,250
Luck: Sorry, no.

138
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:50,590
passerby 1: No wonder.

139
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:53,360
passerby 1: Looks like you just arrived 
from the boonies.

140
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:56,230
passerby 1: I guess it's no surprise you don't know.

141
00:09:56,230 --> 00:09:57,380
Luck: Okay?

142
00:09:57,810 --> 00:10:01,620
passerby 1: It's a statue of the Great Saint Luck!

143
00:10:02,390 --> 00:10:04,790
Luck: Saint... Luck?

144
00:10:05,150 --> 00:10:07,390
passerby 1: A great hero who, ten years ago, 

145
00:10:07,390 --> 00:10:11,110
passerby 1: held off a horde of demons 
by himself inside a dimensional rift!

146
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:13,270
Luck: That's... me?!

147
00:10:13,270 --> 00:10:17,130
passerby 1: His efforts saved the entire world!

148
00:10:17,130 --> 00:10:20,770
passerby 1: Saint Luck, a great hero 
and a great sage!

149
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:25,650
Luck: I bet this means they think 
I died ten years ago.

150
00:10:27,010 --> 00:10:28,520
Luck: Ten years ago?!

151
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:32,270
Luck: I was fighting for an entire decade?

152
00:10:35,550 --> 00:10:38,550
text: ADVENTURERS GUILD HEADQUARTERS

153
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:45,300
adventurer 1: Haven't seen you around before.

154
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:49,870
Luck: Excuse me.

155
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:51,560
adventurer 1: Don't ignore me!

156
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:54,570
adventurer 1: You need to learn 
how things work around—

157
00:11:00,050 --> 00:11:00,820
Luck: Goran!

158
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:11,210
Goran: I'm so happy you came back alive!

159
00:11:11,210 --> 00:11:13,830
Luck: Are you crying? And are you old?

160
00:11:13,830 --> 00:11:17,000
Goran: I'm not cryin'! I have aged!

161
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,460
Goran: We're talking a decade! 
Ten years have passed!

162
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:23,710
Luck: He's bawling.

163
00:11:24,810 --> 00:11:27,090
Luck: These taste good!

164
00:11:27,090 --> 00:11:29,100
Luck: They're so yummy!

165
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:33,060
Luck: Y'know, I haven't eaten 
anything in ten years!

166
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:37,530
Luck: I got all the energy I needed using Drain 
Touch, but my stomach's been empty!

167
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:39,280
Luck: What's the big idea?!

168
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:42,720
Goran: Don't overdo it on solid food 
after a long fast.

169
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:44,610
Goran: Let's get you some rice gruel.

170
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,050
Goran: Hey! Bring some rice gruel!

171
00:11:47,050 --> 00:11:48,200
Goran: On the double!

172
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:55,870
Goran: Still, I'm surprised 
you survived that mess.

173
00:11:55,870 --> 00:11:59,230
Luck: Managing to learn Drain Touch 
made a big difference.

174
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:02,110
Eric: I've brought the rice gruel.

175
00:12:02,110 --> 00:12:03,090
Goran: Enter!

176
00:12:06,590 --> 00:12:09,140
Goran: Oh, you're finally here.

177
00:12:11,910 --> 00:12:14,380
Eric: You're looking well, Luck.

178
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,400
Luck: Eric?

179
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:22,370
Eric: It's... It's good to have you back!

180
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:25,160
Luck: You too, huh?

181
00:12:25,450 --> 00:12:29,760
Luck: What am I supposed to do with 
two crying middle-aged guys?

182
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:33,500
Luck: Looks like even sexy guys have to age.

183
00:12:35,530 --> 00:12:38,680
Eric: Speaking of, Luck. Isn't this unnatural?

184
00:12:38,680 --> 00:12:39,800
Luck: Isn't what?

185
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,760
Goran: Yeah, you haven't aged at all.

186
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:45,710
Goran: In fact, I could swear you got younger.

187
00:12:45,710 --> 00:12:49,120
Luck: Don't be ridiculous. That's not...

188
00:12:50,780 --> 00:12:52,820
Luck: I got younger!

189
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:54,230
Luck: What's going on?!

190
00:12:55,890 --> 00:12:58,940
Luck: When I defeated the 
Demon King with Drain Touch, 

191
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:02,100
Luck: I absorbed a bunch of his life force.

192
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:03,980
Luck: Maybe that's what did it.

193
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:07,230
Luck: What's wrong?

194
00:13:07,230 --> 00:13:09,990
Goran: You defeated the Demon King?!

195
00:13:09,990 --> 00:13:13,490
Luck: Y-Yeah. He revived and showed up again.

196
00:13:16,250 --> 00:13:21,110
Eric: Luck, the kingdom has been 
beefing up its military

197
00:13:21,110 --> 00:13:23,830
Eric: in anticipation of the 
Demon King's recovery and invasion.

198
00:13:23,830 --> 00:13:30,010
Eric: But if you've already defeated him... 
then we owe you some reward.

199
00:13:30,010 --> 00:13:32,260
Goran: You said it, Your Majesty.

200
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:34,760
Luck: "Your Majesty"?

201
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:36,820
Luck: You're the king?!

202
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:38,510
Luck: I mean, I knew you were royalty!

203
00:13:38,510 --> 00:13:43,780
Eric: The previous king felt I deserved it, 
for driving back the Demon King.

204
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:46,800
Goran: Eric is now the king.

205
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:51,540
Goran: And I'm Grand Master of 
the Adventurers Guild.

206
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:54,410
Luck: You two have really done 
well for yourselves.

207
00:13:54,410 --> 00:13:58,470
Goran: Well, you're now a savior 
and a great sage.

208
00:13:58,470 --> 00:14:02,920
Goran: The supreme sorcerer, 
Archduke Luck Franzen.

209
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,070
Luck: Too long!

210
00:14:04,070 --> 00:14:07,320
Luck: And what's with the "archduke"?! 
I'm not nobility!

211
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:08,920
Luck: Who's Franzen?!

212
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:14,060
Eric: I wanted to reward your service, 
so I gave you a noble title.

213
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:17,800
Goran: It was the first thing he did 
after that statue was built.

214
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:20,920
Luck: Oh yeah, the statue! 
What's the story with that?

215
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:23,820
Goran: Oh, you saw it? Lookin' good, isn't he?

216
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:26,560
Luck: Way better than I look.

217
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:30,190
Eric: Well, the sculptor had never met you.

218
00:14:30,550 --> 00:14:34,700
Eric: He made it based on my words and Goran's, 
 and that's how it turned out.

219
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:37,450
Luck: I knew these two were behind it.

220
00:14:37,950 --> 00:14:42,710
Luck: Still, I'm surprised the peerage didn't 
pitch a fit when you made me one of them.

221
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:48,210
Luck: You had no family, and it 
was believed you were dead.

222
00:14:48,670 --> 00:14:54,840
Luck: Doesn't that mean it's going to be a 
problem now that I've come back alive?

223
00:14:56,850 --> 00:15:01,120
Luck: Well, let's not change 
the official story that Luck is dead.

224
00:15:01,730 --> 00:15:02,910
Goran: Luck...

225
00:15:03,370 --> 00:15:05,730
Eric: Then, what will you do now?

226
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,940
Luck: It's a good opportunity.

227
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:10,590
Luck: I'll start over from square one 
as an adventurer.

228
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:18,010
Luck: Wow.

229
00:15:18,010 --> 00:15:19,990
Goran: There's your new adventurer card.

230
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:26,060
Goran: We used an info-masking spell 
so that only the name "Lock" appears.

231
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:27,750
Luck: Where did "Lock" come from?

232
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:31,680
Goran: Your real name is Luck Lock Franzen.

233
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,750
Luck: They even gave me a middle name?

234
00:15:34,030 --> 00:15:39,330
Goran: Your first job of 
"S-Rank Supreme Sorcerer" is hidden, 

235
00:15:39,330 --> 00:15:44,060
Goran: so only your second job of 
"F-Rank Warrior" shows up.

236
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:49,770
Goran: From now on, you'll be known 
as Lock, the F-rank warrior.

237
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:52,780
Luck: Sorry to make you do all this.

238
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:56,940
Goran: Sure, but won't you get bored 
starting over from square one?

239
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:58,540
Goran: You could fight stronger enemies.

240
00:15:59,530 --> 00:16:03,320
Goran: I've already fought plenty 
of strong enemies.

241
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:07,040
Butler: Saint Lu... Master Lock.

242
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:09,920
Butler: I was terribly rude to you the other day.

243
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:13,420
Lock: That's okay. I mean, 
I wasn't very presentable.

244
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:15,400
Butler: You are too kind.

245
00:16:15,970 --> 00:16:17,300
Butler: Where are you headed?

246
00:16:17,610 --> 00:16:19,560
Lock: To the Adventurers Guild.

247
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:21,320
Butler: Until later, then.

248
00:16:26,150 --> 00:16:29,260
Arone: Hello. I am Arone, the receptionist.

249
00:16:29,850 --> 00:16:31,210
Lock: I'd like to do this.

250
00:16:31,210 --> 00:16:32,320
Arone: All right.

251
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:35,300
Arone: Goblin extermination.

252
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:36,570
Arone: By yourself?

253
00:16:36,570 --> 00:16:38,820
Lock: Yes, that's the plan.

254
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:43,480
Arone: It's dangerous for a rookie to 
solo a goblin-extermination job.

255
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,070
Arone: I cannot recommend it.

256
00:16:45,070 --> 00:16:47,740
Lock: I know, but I'll be fine.

257
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:50,330
Lock: I'm really S-rank anyway.

258
00:16:50,330 --> 00:16:54,820
Arone: It's not uncommon for rookies to die 
because they underestimate goblins.

259
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:55,590
Lock: Right...

260
00:16:55,590 --> 00:16:57,750
Arone: I cannot recommend going solo.

261
00:16:57,750 --> 00:16:59,820
Ario: Would you like to come with us?

262
00:17:01,070 --> 00:17:03,310
Ario: We're F-rank adventurers too.

263
00:17:03,310 --> 00:17:05,329
Ario: A mage and a bow scout.

264
00:17:05,329 --> 00:17:07,369
Ario: We could use someone on the front line.

265
00:17:07,369 --> 00:17:09,480
Ginny: You're a warrior, right?

266
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,930
Arone: A wonderful idea!

267
00:17:10,930 --> 00:17:13,490
Arone: You three will exterminate goblins! 
Approved!

268
00:17:13,869 --> 00:17:16,160
Lock: Huh? But I never said I'd—

269
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,609
Arone: It is a wonderful idea!

270
00:17:18,609 --> 00:17:19,740
Lock: Yes, ma'am.

271
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,640
Lock: Well...

272
00:17:22,109 --> 00:17:24,800
Lock: It's important to train rookies, too.

273
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:32,480
Ario: Well met. My name's Ario.

274
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:34,400
Ario: I can use Fireball.

275
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,020
Ario: This is my younger sister Ginny.

276
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:38,800
Ario: Ginny here. I have our 
archery needs covered.

277
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:42,800
Lock: I'm Lock. I use a sword. 
Nice to meet you.

278
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:06,560
Ginny: Losses include two months' worth of 
stored crops, two cows, and three sheep.

279
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:11,710
Ginny: The western fencing often gets damaged, 
so they probably come from that direction.

280
00:18:12,050 --> 00:18:17,220
Ario: So, based on goblin habitat ranges, 
the den is...

281
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:20,030
Ginny: The evidence suggests there 
are about ten of them.

282
00:18:20,030 --> 00:18:21,840
Ario: Yeah, thereabouts.

283
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:30,470
Ginny: This way. I don't think 
it's far from here.

284
00:18:30,470 --> 00:18:32,360
Ario: Okay, let's go.

285
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:35,880
Lock: Ginny is quite a skilled scout.

286
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:38,960
Lock: She sticks to the hunt, 
and she's quick-witted.

287
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:41,080
Lock: She doesn't seem like an F-rank to me.

288
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:42,860
Lock: But...

289
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:46,210
Lock: They've misjudged how 
many goblins there are.

290
00:18:47,030 --> 00:18:50,140
Lock: They haven't noticed 
the camouflaged footprints.

291
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:52,650
Lock: And it's important to note, 

292
00:18:52,650 --> 00:18:55,770
Lock: goblins aren't clever enough 
to hide their footprints.

293
00:18:56,390 --> 00:19:00,080
Lock: In other words, there's some 
other monster leading them.

294
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,070
Lock: Ginny.

295
00:19:02,710 --> 00:19:04,010
Ginny: What's up?

296
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:07,770
Lock: Nah, never mind.

297
00:19:08,570 --> 00:19:10,830
Ario: What's the holdup, you two?

298
00:19:10,830 --> 00:19:11,690
Ginny: Okay!

299
00:19:11,690 --> 00:19:13,290
Ginny: Let's go, Lock.

300
00:19:15,150 --> 00:19:20,200
Lock: You don't train someone by 
telling them everything in advance.

301
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:22,900
Lock: There's a lot you can learn from failure.

302
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:24,710
Lock: Especially while you're young.

303
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:29,830
Lock: But now that I've chosen not to tell them, 
the responsibility is mine.

304
00:19:30,710 --> 00:19:33,690
Lock: I swear I won't let these two die.

305
00:19:37,490 --> 00:19:39,610
Ginny: That must be the den.

306
00:19:39,610 --> 00:19:41,800
Ario: Looks like an old mine shaft.

307
00:19:42,550 --> 00:19:44,310
Lock: This looks bad.

308
00:19:44,310 --> 00:19:45,830
Ginny: It does?

309
00:19:45,830 --> 00:19:47,720
Ario: I don't think so.

310
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:52,220
Ario: Goblins are nocturnal.
We should attack while it's still daytime.

311
00:19:52,220 --> 00:19:53,780
Lock: I'll take the lead.

312
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:55,850
Lock: Ginny, give me covering fire.

313
00:19:55,850 --> 00:19:58,560
Lock: Once we're in there, guard our rear.

314
00:19:58,560 --> 00:19:59,860
Ginny: Will do.

315
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:04,000
Lock: Ario, conserve your magic 
as much as possible as we go.

316
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:04,900
Ario: All right.

317
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:05,800
Lock: Let's go!

318
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:36,010
Ario: We've already defeated 
over thirty of them.

319
00:20:36,510 --> 00:20:39,230
Ginny: Isn't that more than we expected?

320
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:43,590
Lock: Packs like this are often 
led by a hobgoblin.

321
00:20:46,270 --> 00:20:49,580
Lock: Ario, can you still launch Fireball?

322
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:53,190
Ario: If I push really hard. 
But I'm nearly spent.

323
00:20:53,190 --> 00:20:55,440
Lock: Ginny, you have enough arrows?

324
00:20:56,010 --> 00:20:58,350
Ginny: I only have three left.

325
00:20:59,350 --> 00:21:00,880
Ario: Let's withdraw.

326
00:21:01,110 --> 00:21:02,120
Ginny: But!

327
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:05,460
Ario: It's dangerous to push on ahead when 
we're low on magic and arrows.

328
00:21:06,770 --> 00:21:08,290
Lock: Good decision.

329
00:21:09,010 --> 00:21:11,040
Ginny: Okay, fine.

330
00:21:23,530 --> 00:21:25,320
Lock: A goblin lord.

331
00:21:28,230 --> 00:21:29,440
Lock: It's strange.

332
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:32,320
Lock: The way they steal livestock 
a little at a time

333
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:36,450
Lock: means the one in charge is giving 
systematic orders to the goblins.

334
00:21:36,450 --> 00:21:38,540
Lock: That suggests a certain 
level of intelligence.

335
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:43,310
Lock: But I don't sense that at all 
from that goblin lord.

336
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:47,010
Lock: There must be something else 
calling the shots after all.

337
00:21:56,930 --> 00:21:58,180
Sia: Pipsqueak!

338
00:21:59,740 --> 00:22:01,180
Sia: Stay out of my way!

339
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:02,860
Sia: Or else!

340
00:22:05,110 --> 00:22:07,110
Credits: TRANSLATION: DUANE JOHNSON

341
00:22:07,110 --> 00:22:10,110
Credits: TIMING: EDGAR CRUZ
EDITING: ZACHARY CARLYSLE

342
00:22:10,110 --> 00:22:13,110
Credits: QUALITY CONTROL: GABRIELLA ALABANZA
TRANSLATION CHECK: SRIRAM GURUNATHAN

343
00:23:34,950 --> 00:23:40,030
text (top): NEXT TIME: THERE WAS A FORMIDABLE FOE
DEEP INSIDE THE DEN
